 interviews last Friday, viewing adoption as a way to build her family, give back, and show love and acceptance.\n  - Family building: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday, expressing excitement about building a family and giving a home to needy children through adoption.\n  - adoption journey: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday, a major step toward her goal of building a family and giving a home to needy kids.\n  - council meeting for adoption: Caroline attended a council meeting for adoption last Friday; it was inspiring, emotional, and reinforced her determination to adopt.\n  - Mel: Melanie (Mel) congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews. She supports Caroline's goal of building a family through adoption to help needy kids.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - child: Caroline applied to adoption agencies this week, taking the first step towards becoming a mom, with help from an adoption advice/assistance group.\n  - mom: Caroline is taking the first step toward becoming a mom by applying to adoption agencies after attending an adoption advice/assistance group.\n  - adoption advice/assistance group: Caroline attended an adoption advice/assistance group this week to get help for her decision to apply to adoption agencies to become a mom.\n  - adoption process: Caroline mentioned an adoption process and Melanie expressed support and asked about what Caroline is excited for regarding it.\n  - the future: Caroline is excited for the future after taking the first step toward becoming a mom by applying to adoption agencies with help from an advice group.\n  - references: Caroline mentioned that references are documents needed when preparing for adoption, alongside financial info and medical checks.\n  - adoption agencies: Caroline is preparing to adopt, seeking advice on finding adoption agencies or lawyers, gathering documents, and preparing emotionally for the process.\n  - medical checks: Medical checks are required documents needed when adopting, along with references and financial information, as advised by Caroline.\n  - kids: Melanie's son was in a scary road trip accident but is now okay. Melanie mentioned her kids enjoyed an activity they did yesterday to relax after the trip. Caroline is passionate about helping kids through adoption.\n  - these kids: Caroline is excited to build a family and give a loving, safe home to 'these kids' through adoption, ensuring they experience love and acceptance.\n  - LGBTQ+ folks with adoption: Caroline chose an organization because they help LGBTQ+ folks with adoption, valuing their inclusivity and support.\n  - Oscar: Oscar is Caroline's guinea pig, mentioned to Melanie when discussing her adoption plans and showing a picture of him eating parsley.\n  - next time: Melanie asked Caroline what she hopes to do for the next time, following Caroline's volunteering experience.\n  - lawyer: A lawyer can help with the adoption process and provide necessary information, alongside an adoption agency.\n  - support and encouragement: Caroline appreciated Melanie's support and encouragement regarding her talk on her transgender journey, which aimed to inspire others and promote inclusivity.\n  - paintings: Caroline is preparing to show her paintings at an LGBTQ art show next month. She mentioned this when asking Melanie about creative outlets.\n  - love, acceptance, and hope: Melanie thanked Caroline for using her voice to create love, acceptance, and hope after Caroline shared her transgender journey.\n  - who I really am: Caroline found out who she really is with invaluable help from friends, family, and mentors during tough times, and now wants to pass that support to others.\n  - gender identity: Caroline mentioned that creating art, like painting and drawing, was important during h