nd a form of self-care, often accompanied by music and wine.\n  - favorite dish: Andrew asked Audrey if she has a favorite dish made with garlic and requested the recipe.\n  - recetas: Audrey enjoys experimenting with and trying new recipes in the kitchen as a way to de-stress and let creativity flow.\n  - this dish: Audrey finds cooking and eating 'this dish' rewarding, considering it self-care while listening to music and drinking wine.\n  - the nature: Andrew enjoyed a refreshing picnic in nature with his girlfriend last Friday. Audrey also likes being in nature and mentioned having a good walk with her dogs.\n  - a glass of wine: Audrey pours a glass of wine while cooking and eating, describing it as therapeutic self-care.\n  - snacks: Audrey will bring snacks on Saturday for an activity and is super excited.\n  - goodies: Audrey made some 'goodies' recently using recycled objects to thank her neighbors for their pup-friendly homes.\n  - Audrey's fur babies: Audrey has four fur babies she considers more important than anything. Her existing summary notes they have distinct personalities: relaxed oldest, second likes games, third is naughty but cuddly, and youngest is adventurous.\n  - cool stuff: Audrey mentioned that there will be some cool stuff happening today.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - friends: Audrey meets with other dog owners weekly for tips and playdates for her four pups. Andrew values friends for support, and Audrey values friendship.\n  - books: Andrew reads books about ecological systems. Audrey mentioned that books like that must be really interesting and asked what Andrew has discovered from reading them.\n  - furry buddies: Andrew hopes Audrey and her furry buddies go on some fun adventures soon.\n  - muffins: Andrew and his girlfriend tried delicious muffins along with croissants and tarts at a new cafe scene in the 