ire others.\n  - mentoring: Caroline finds the mentoring program rewarding, supporting amazing, resilient, and strong young folks; the experience is going great.\n  - mental health: Melanie stated that being yourself is important for mental health and finding peace. Caroline thanked Melanie for the insight.\n  - supportive community of hope: Caroline aims to build a strong, supportive community of hope by sharing her journey and experiences to promote understanding and acceptance.\n  - love, acceptance, and hope: Melanie thanked Caroline for using her voice to create love, acceptance, and hope after Caroline shared her transgender journey.\n  - advocacy: Caroline plans to attend a transgender conference this month to learn more about advocacy and meet others in the community.\n  - career options: Caroline is excited about continuing her education and checking out career options.\n  - support and encouragement: Caroline appreciated Melanie's support and encouragement regarding her talk on her transgender journey, which aimed to inspire others and promote inclusivity.\n  - Volunteering: Caroline volunteers at an LGBTQ+ youth center, which she finds gratifying and will continue, focusing on community and support.\n  - LGBTQ+ folks with adoption: Caroline chose an organization because they help LGBTQ+ folks with adoption, valuing their inclusivity and support.\n  - courage to transition: Caroline stated that realizing she could be herself without fear and having the courage to transition was the best part, calling it freeing to express herself authentically with support.\n  - LGBTQ advocacy stuff: Melanie asked Caroline about any upcoming exciting LGBTQ advocacy stuff after discussing Caroline's positive mentoring experiences.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - gender identity: Caroline mentioned that creating ar