ned from San Francisco with insights on car modification, finding satisfaction in fixing and improving old cars to help others.\n  - Dave: Dave, who is restoring a vintage Mustang engine, has taken up photography, focusing on local scenery. He discussed his photography and the car project with Calvin.\n  - cars: Dave believes attention to detail in vehicles makes a big impact, echoing his views on music. Calvin relates to stress from car servicing; Dave finds restoring cars fulfilling.\n  - machines: Dave has been fascinated with how machines work since he was ten, beginning his interest by fixing an old car.\n  - car project: Dave inspired others with a blog post about how he made his car look like a beast. His prior work involved a vintage Mustang's engine.\n  - Dave: Dave attended a car workshop in San Francisco to learn car restoration techniques. He also had a card night with friends last Friday and discussed his ongoing car restoration project with Calvin.\n  - car maintenance shop: Dave's car maintenance shop lost a deal they pursued for months to a competing shop, making Dave feel bummed out despite his hard work.\n  - auto engineering: Dave's fascination with auto engineering started at age ten after fixing an old car, leading to a lifelong interest in transforming broken-down cars to high-running ones. Calvin is also into cars and making powerful models.\n  - skills: Dave attributes the opening of his car maintenance shop to his skills and hard work paying off, which he finds incredible.\n  - Dave: Dave congratulated Calvin on his album release and expressed enthusiasm for live music. Dave invited Calvin to see his cool cars in his garage.\n  - Dave: Dave's band had a fun rehearsal session last night. Last weekend, Dave attended a rock concert in Boston. Dave is also praised by Calvin for fixing cars.\n  - Dave: Dave previously enjoyed a card night and is restoring a car for his auto engineering goal. He chatted with Calvin about Calvin's amazing performance on a big stage.\n  - car show: Dave's interest in cars began at age 10 when his dad took him to his first car show, leading him to become an automotive engineer.\n  - people working on your car: Dave asked Calvin about the people working on his car, inquiring if Calvin feels confident in their skills and knowledge.\n  - dad: Dave's dad took him to his first car show when he was 10, which sparked his interest in cars. Dave later became an automotive engineer.\n  - car: Dave posted on his blog about modifying his car; Calvin asked where Dave got the car after Calvin's party discussion.\n  - car modification: Dave told Calvin his car modification was a lot of work but worth it, after Calvin praised Dave's blog inspiring creativity.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2073,"context_chars":8277,"retrieval_duration":0.16972851753234863,"response_duration":2.5859978199005127,"total_duration":2.7557263374328613,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions that Dave works on all kinds of cars and includes the aspect of full restorations of classic cars, which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides comprehensive information about the types of cars Dave works on at his shop. It explicitly states that he works on 'all kinds of cars' and performs 'full restorations on classic cars,' which aligns perfectly with the golden answer. Additionally, the context includes details about regular maintenance and specific examples of cars he is working on, further supporting the completeness of the information.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["all kinds of cars","full restorations of classic cars","regular maintenance on cars"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_3","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_3_qa_49","category":"1","difficulty":"unknown","query":"How many times has Joanna's scripts been rejected?","golden_answer":"Twice","hypothesis":"Joanna has experienced rejecti