d rejections from a film contest, which Nate acknowledged as tough but encouraged her to keep trying.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - love story: Joanna is writing a movie script for a love story that involves many challenges; she is working hard and hopes to see it on the big screen.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n  - research: Joanna has been doing non-stop research and networking for something she is determined to make happen.\n  - people: Joanna shared how rewarding it was to see her written work performed, drawing inspiration from real life and imagination to create characters.\n  - writer: Joanna, identified as a writer, experienced a major setback when her laptop crashed, resulting in the loss of all her work.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - road-trip script: Joanna is filming her own movie based on the road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and feels it is full of potential to show her vision.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - book: Joanna fini