s to keep them busy, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek.\n  - her pups: One of Audrey's pups pulled so hard on the leash last Friday at the park that it busted; she chased and caught the pup. Audrey calmed her by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly.\n  - photos: Andrew asked Audrey for photos from her recent activity. Audrey will take photos featuring autumn colors, which she previously shared pictures of her fluffy, groomed pups.\n  - outdoor pics: Audrey requested Andrew share awesome outdoor pics and tell her about his hike.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - there: Audrey mentioned she'd love to take her dogs to 'there' sometime, following an appointment with an animal behaviorist.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - tattoo parlor: Audrey went to the tattoo parlor to get more drawings added to her existing tattoo of her four dogs.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - pups: Audrey's pups got groomed at the pet salon last Friday, and they looked cute with shiny coats. Audrey worries about them in new places, but they were good.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - Andrew (assistant): Andrew asked Audrey about the tips she received from her dogs' appointment with an animal behaviorist. Andrew suggested visiting a lake near a trail to see the autumn colors.\n  - rewards: Audrey is looking forward to learning how to train her pets better and believes they will learn quickly because they love rewards.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1988,"context_chars":7519,"retrieval_duration":0.23601555824279785,"response_duration":2.734856128692627,"total_dur