ion: Audrey suggests adding creative mental stimulation to keep dogs happy in the city, alongside socialization and daily exercise.\n  - city dogs: Audrey's city dogs love trying new parks and trails and go on adventures very often.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - tips on taking care of Toby: Audrey offered Andrew tips on taking care of Toby, mentioning daily brushing, regular baths, and nail trims are essential for mountain life.\n  - paws: Audrey pays attention to sensitive areas like ears and paws during gentle grooming, emphasizing patience and positivity.\n  - Audrey's fur kids: Audrey's fur kids were taken to the pet salon, where they got groomed, looked cute, and were well-behaved in the new environment.\n  - hide-and-seek: Audrey gives her four pups activities to keep them busy, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek.\n  - flowers: Audrey's flowers look great, according to Andrew. Audrey previously mentioned her veggie patch is growing.\n  - Audrey's fur babies: Audrey has four fur babies she considers more important than anything. Her existing summary notes they have distinct personalities: relaxed oldest, second likes games, third is naughty but cuddly, and youngest is adventurous.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - breed: Andrew asked Audrey about her dogs' breed and what they enjoy doing most, following a discussion about dog training and finding dog-friendly spots.\n  - Audrey (as