icks like sit, stay, shake, and roll over, which is fun and rewarding.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - Audrey's fur kids: Audrey's fur kids were taken to the pet salon, where they got groomed, looked cute, and were well-behaved in the new environment.\n  - rewards: Audrey is looking forward to learning how to train her pets better and believes they will learn quickly because they love rewards.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - Positive reinforcement: Audrey is using positive reinforcement techniques, suggested by an animal behaviorist after an appointment last Wednesday, to help with her dogs' behavioral issues.\n  - animal behaviorist: Audrey saw an animal behaviorist last Wednesday due to her dogs' abnormal behavior; she received tips and is now using positive reinforcement techniques.\n  - pic of them after the grooming: Audrey learned grooming her pups herself, making her closer to them. Andrew requested a photo of the pups after the grooming to see how adorable they look.\n  - passion: Audrey's passion involves making jewelry from recycled objects. Andrew finds it amazing how this passion is used to make a difference.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - puppy: Andrew adopted a new puppy named Toby. Andrew shared photos of his puppy playing in the park, which made Andrew and Audrey happy.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2010,"context_chars":8020,"retrieval_duration":0.13636183738708496,"response_duration":3.22946