ustom exhaust and performance upgrades) into a masterpiece.\n  - Dave: Dave attended a car workshop in San Francisco to learn car restoration techniques. He also had a card night with friends last Friday and discussed his ongoing car restoration project with Calvin.\n  - Dave: Dave's band had a fun rehearsal session last night. Last weekend, Dave attended a rock concert in Boston. Dave is also praised by Calvin for fixing cars.\n  - Dave: Dave recently returned from San Francisco with insights on car modification, finding satisfaction in fixing and improving old cars to help others.\n  - car stuff: Dave is tied up with car stuff, recently returned from San Francisco with knowledge on car modification. He listens to vinyl while working on cars to relax and stay productive.\n  - performance upgrades: Dave restored and modified a car, adding a custom exhaust and performance upgrades, which he is proud of.\n  - junkyard: Dave found a Ford Mustang in a junkyard; the car was in bad shape but had potential for restoration.\n  - car restoration: Dave restored and modified a car himself, adding a custom exhaust and performance upgrades. Calvin congratulated Dave on his awesome job and skills.\n  - Dave (assistant): Dave opened his own car maintenance shop, teaming up with a local garage, and is enjoying sharing his car knowledge with awesome mechanics.\n  - classic car: Calvin discussed restoring a classic car, which required skill and determination, to Dave.\n  - Dave: Dave, who is restoring a vintage Mustang engine, has taken up photography, focusing on local scenery. He discussed his photography and the car project with Calvin.\n  - Dave: Dave is fascinated by how machines work, starting at age ten after fixing an old car. He enjoys car engineering and transforming broken-down vehicles into high-running ones.\n  - Dave: Dave asked Calvin about his car post-crash, mentioned arranging regular walks with friends in parks, and commented on a mansion's stunning view in Japan.\n  - custom exhaust: Dave added a custom exhaust and performance upgrades to a car he restored and modified, which he is proud of and gives it a sweet sound.\n  - classic muscle car: Dave is working on a classic muscle car, modifying it to have a modern vibe while retaining its classic style. He is learning auto engineering for this project.\n  - car maintenance shop: Dave's car maintenance shop lost a deal they pursued for months to a competing shop, making Dave feel bummed out despite his hard work.\n  - cars: Dave shared a picture of his latest car project, which Calvin found inspiring, contrasting it with Calvin's music endeavors. Dave finds working on cars therapeutic.\n  - classic cars: Dave opened his car maintenance shop, fulfilling a dream. He works on all kinds of cars, including full restorations of classic cars.\n  - Dave: Dave recently returned from a road trip with friends, enjoying the countryside and recharging. This trip reminded him of his passion, which makes long work hours worthwhile.\n  - engine: Dave restored and modified a car, adding a custom exhaust and performance upgrades. He mentioned tinkering with engines in his dad's garage as a child, relating it to a passion and job.\n  - car mod workshop: Dave attended a car mod workshop in San Francisco to learn about car restoration techniques and pursue his passion for auto engineering and custom car building.\n  - car: Dave posted on his blog about modifying his car; Calvin asked where Dave got the car after Calvin's party discussion.\n  - car project: Dave inspired others with a blog post about how he made his car look like a beast. His prior work involved a vintage Mustang's engine.\n  - Dave: Dave congratulated Calvin on his album release and expressed enthusiasm for live music. Dave invited Calvin to see his cool cars in his garage.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2033,"context_chars":8102,"retrieval_duration":0.13183045387268066,"response_duration":2.3198418617248535,"total_duration":2.45