ery morning and evening, valuing exercise and nature.\n  - them: Jolene has been doing 'them' sporadically for about 3 years and they have had a real positive effect on her.\n  - lake: Jolene is attending a meditation course at a retreat near a lake. Previously, Jolene captured a photo of a lake surrounded by trees, noting its peacefulness.\n  - exams: Jolene has many finals coming up this month, which is stressful, and she plans to take a trip to relax afterward.\n  - destination: Deborah mentioned that the journey is as important as the destination, encouraging Jolene to take time for herself and find joy in it.\n  - Jolene's partner: Jolene's partner has values that encourage pursuing creative endeavors. They recently returned from a trip to Rio de Janeiro with Jolene, where they tried yoga classes.\n  - creation: Deborah mentioned a creation to Jolene, relating it to someone special's grace and strength when facing hardships.\n  - Avalanche: Jolene read \"Avalanche\" by Neal Stephenson in one sitting two weeks ago.\n  - park: Deborah likes a park near her house with a forest trail and beach where she does yoga and reflects; it contains a special bench.\n  - park with a forest trail: Deborah's favorite location is a park with a forest trail because it is calming to get lost in nature there.\n  - someone close to Jolene: Someone close to Jolene used to bake cookies with her.\n  - Susie: Jolene mentioned that Susie is a great companion. Jolene has had Susie for two years.\n  - video games: Jolene shared that her passion for video games started when her parents got her something related when she was 10 years old.\n  - walks: Deborah suggested taking walks as a helpful self-care activity for finding work-life balance. Jolene mentioned Deborah takes photos during her walks.\n  - forest trail: Deborah loves going to a park near her house that has a forest trail and a beach, finding it a peaceful spot for yoga and reflection.\n  - garden: Deborah visits the garden, whic