ne spot he wants others to check out.\n  - backyard: Calvin has a backyard at his Japanese mansion, which offers a view of a gorgeous sunset over the river.\n  - hobbies: Dave enjoys hobbies. Calvin relaxes by working on his Ferrari and converting a Japanese mansion into a recording studio, following his trip to Japan and meeting artists in Boston.\n  - friends: Calvin shared that friends were present at the party he threw at his Japanese house last week for his new album, showing much love.\n  - show in Japan: Calvin had an amazing experience touring with a well-known artist, concluding with a show in Japan.\n  - Japan: Calvin had an incredible trip to Japan, finding the culture and people cool and longing to return; it was an experience worth the hard work.\n  - Japanese artists: Calvin is working on music collaborations with Japanese artists and is excited about the outcome.\n  - Japanese culture: Calvin is stuck with his music creativity but is loving getting to know Japanese culture.\n  - octopus: Calvin has a favorite item custom-made by a Japanese artist friend featuring an octopus, symbolizing his love for art and the sea.\n  - taking a break: Calvin is taking a break to get his mojo back, following Dave's advice to explore.\n  - Tokyo: Dave plans to explore Shibuya and Shinjuku in Tokyo. Calvin plans to try something new while in Tokyo.\n  - microphone: Calvin saved his favorite microphone after his place flooded. Dave expressed sympathy and offered help. Calvin recently toured with Frank Ocean.\n  - Calvin: Calvin had an inspiring chat with an artist about music and art, feeling a creative high. He and Dave previously planned to meet when Dave is in Boston. Dave has taken up photography.\n  - Dave: Dave recently took up photography, focusing on scenery. He chatted with Calvin about a photo Calvin shared, congratulated him on an amazing-looking event, and acknowledged Calvin's plan to visit Boston.\n  - blogging: Dave recently started a blog about car mods 