anie mentioned that figurines she bought remind her of family love. Caroline is pursuing adoption to build a family.\n  - Mel: Melanie (Mel) congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews. She supports Caroline's goal of building a family through adoption to help needy kids.\n  - loved ones: Melanie's son was in a scary road trip accident; both Melanie and Caroline affirmed the importance of loved ones and family after this event.\n  - home: Caroline hopes to build her own family and put a roof over kids who haven't had one. Melanie noted that giving a home to needy kids is a loving way to build a family.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - Melanie's daughter: Melanie celebrated her daughter's birthday last night with a concert. Melanie mentioned seeing her daughter's smiles was awesome.\n  - family mems: Caroline made new family memories recently, which she discussed with Melanie.\n  - move: Caroline asked Melanie about her family's support during her move.\n  - support and encouragement: Caroline appreciated Melanie's support and encouragement regarding her talk on her transgender journey, which aimed to inspire others and promote inclusivity.\n  - family camping trip: Melanie looks forward to the annual family camping trip, which involves roasting marshmallows and telling stories around the campfire, as a summer highlight.\n  - me-time: Melanie carves out daily me-time for running, reading, or playing the violin to refresh herself and stay present for her family.\n  - research: Melanie is going to do research and ready herself emotionally regarding adoption, based on a tip from Caroline.\n  - Family time: Melanie recounted a scary road trip where her son was in an accident, which served as a reminder to cherish family time.\n  - their brother: Melanie's son was in an accident during a road tri