on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - explore new things: Joanna encouraged Nate to step outside his comfort zone and explore new things, stating the rewards can be great.\n  - exploring nature: Joanna enjoys exploring nature as one of her hobbies, alongside writing, reading, and watching movies.\n  - research: Joanna has been doing non-stop research and networking for something she is determined to make happen.\n  - new things: Joanna submitted a screenplay to a film contest and mentioned that people love it when she makes them new things.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - new one: Nate asked Joanna about the topic of the \"new one\" after mentioning he baked desserts and made ice cream for a friend.\n  - simpler times: Joanna stated that 'simpler times' bring back memories, but it is nice to create new memories while growing up.\n  - identity: Joanna is writing a personal story about loss, identity, and connection which she has had for ages but recently found the courage to write.\n  - new memories: Joanna stated to Nate to keep making great memories and supporting each other, and to keep reaching for their dreams.\n  - Woodhaven: Joanna visited Woodhaven for a road trip; seeing how much the town changed sparked ideas for her next movie script. Woodhaven has an interesting past with cool people.\n  - \"Finding Home\": \"Finding Home\" is a script Joanna is writing with her writers group about a girl's journey to find her true home. She finds the work rewarding and emotional.\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n</ENTI